KNOWN GAP, owned by `a-composed-recipe-segment-arrives-without-its-lines`.

The same shape as `a-touch-over-a-composed-recipes-marked-line` under `-q`,
where the answer rather than the disk is what moves. GNU Make runs the marked
lines it meets before the first unmarked one and reads their status; Ronin's
segment is one launch that never runs, so it answers without running anything.

GNU Make 4.4.1 writes `before.out` and exits 1. Ronin exits 1 having written
nothing. Decided on `pretending-over-an-assembled-recipe`.
